<title>BELGIUM: EU vets Thyssen/Cardo railway deal.</title>
<headline>EU vets Thyssen/Cardo railway deal.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said it was starting a preliminary review of a proposed joint venture between Swedish engineering and machinery group Cardo AB and Thyssen Industrie Ag to which they would transfer their railway activities.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that the deal was submitted for clearance on October 8 under the European Union's merger rules. The rules prohibit creation or strengthening of dominant positions.</p>
<p>The Commission has a month from the notification date to clear the operation or start an in-depth probe.</p>
<p>Thyssen Industrie is a subsidiary of Thyssen AG active in components for the railway industry and rail brakes. -- Brussels newsroom 322 2876841</p>
</text>
